Host-side tests for the D64 REL file support
=============================================

This directory contains a small test harness that compiles the firmware
source (src/d64ops.c) for the host by shadowing the AVR-specific headers
with the shims in shims/ and linking it against stubs.c, which emulates
the image access layer with an in-memory copy of a D64 file. harness.c
includes d64ops.c directly to reach its internal functions and emulates
the bus protocol of iec.c (refill on EOI and buffer wrap for REL files).

Running the tests
-----------------

    make check      generates test images (blank.d64 and multi.d64 via
                    d64lib.py, blank.d71, blank.d81 and c1541.d64 via the
                    c1541 tool from VICE, looked up on PATH; set
                    C1541=... to use a different binary) and runs the
                    CRUD tests against them
    make validate   verifies the resulting disk images independently
                    with the Python code in d64lib.py/validate.py
    make clean      removes build products and test images

The CRUD tests cover creating REL files, reading and writing records
(including records that span sector boundaries and record length 254),
seeking with the P command, growth past the end of the file, appending,
reopening (including the record length mismatch error), scratching,
files without data sectors (opening, record length mismatch, growth and
scratch) and reading a file created by c1541 itself. validate.py checks
the on-disk side sector and data sector chains, BAM allocation and
directory entry contents, and cross-checks selected files with c1541.

Note that these tests exercise the logic of the REL implementation, but
they do not replace a firmware build: compile for real hardware with
"make CONFIG=..." before flashing.
